# Reproduction
`python3 analysis/wealth_disparity_analysis.py` (seed 20261023, B=10,000 bootstrap) writes:
- table1_cell_medians_1985.csv - median + bootstrap 95% CI, n, share-zero, share-negative, mean, p25, p75, thin-cell flags, for every race x sex cell in both ever_jailed groups
- table2_within_stratum_gaps_1985.csv - within-stratum jailed-minus-not dollar gaps with bootstrap CIs, ratio, Mann-Whitney p, Cliff's delta, % of replicates jailed<not, role (PRIMARY vs DESCRIPTIVE)
- table2b_ratio_bootstrap.csv - ratio CIs + fraction of replicates with non-zero denominator
- table3_within_incarcerated.csv - race contrasts at matched sex inside the incarcerated group + pooled women-vs-men
- table4_transform_sensitivity_men.csv - as-recorded vs zero-floor vs top-1% winsorised
- table5_dedup_sensitivity_men.csv - headline vs de-duplicated (1,899 rows / 50 jailed respondents dropped)
- table6_year_trend_men.csv - 1985/1990/1996 persistence (secondary context)
- table7_quantile_gaps_men.csv - p25/p50/p75/p90 gaps
- run_log.txt / stdout.txt - full console log
Note: 'hipanic' is the raw misspelled label for Hispanic in the source file (3 race categories, not 4);
display mapping only. Raw negatives and zeros in composite_wealth_1985 are retained (net wealth, debt allowed).
